#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The autumn feast thanked the gods for the harvest, before the long winter."
msgstr "På høstfesten takket man gudene for avlingen, før den lange vinteren."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Tipsy Uncle"
msgstr "Den lystige onkelen"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Uncle Sven of Frosttorp sang and danced all night, and now he can't find his way home! He is very "
"merry and a little wobbly. Row him home to Arne, please."
msgstr ""
"Onkel Sven fra Frosttorp sang og danset hele natta, og nå finner han ikke veien hjem! Han er "
"veldig lystig og litt ustø. Ro ham hjem til Arne, er {crew|du|du|dere} snill{crew|||e}."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Uncle Sven! Singing all the way, I hear? Come in, sleep it off. Thank you, girls!"
msgstr ""
"Onkel Sven! Sang hele veien, hører jeg? Kom inn og sov ut rusen. Takk skal {crew|du|du|dere} ha!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Uncle Sven: Ho ho! Two little vikings with a boat! Let us sing on the way!"
msgstr ""
"Onkel Sven: Ho ho! {crew|En liten viking|En liten viking|To små vikinger} med båt! La oss synge på"
" veien!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sven"
msgstr "Sven"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
