#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/048_geese_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Geese were kept on viking farms for eggs, feathers and down for pillows."
msgstr "Vikingene holdt gjess for egg, fjær og dun til puter."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Runestone"
msgstr "Runesteinen"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"I will raise a runestone for my mother. The stone comes from the quarry by Bergö, and the "
"runecarver needs iron chisels from the smith. The stone is so big, it takes three crates of room!"
msgstr ""
"Jeg vil reise en runestein for mora mi. Steinen kommer fra steinbruddet ved Bergö, og runeristeren"
" trenger meisler av jern fra smeden. Steinen er så stor at den tar plass som tre kasser!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Good chisels. Now the stone."
msgstr "Gode meisler. Nå steinen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The stone! The carver begins today."
msgstr "Steinen! Runeristeren begynner i dag."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "It is in three pieces, to fit in your boat. The carver joins them."
msgstr ""
"Den er i tre biter, så den får plass i båten {crew|din|din|deres}. Runeristeren setter dem sammen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The runestone stands! It says: Eirik raised this stone for Gunnvor, his good mother. And at the "
"bottom, small: Ylva and Sigrid rowed it."
msgstr ""
"Runesteinen står! Der står det: Eirik reiste denne steinen etter Gunnvor, sin gode mor. Og "
"nederst, med små tegn: Ylva og Sigrid rodde den."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Stone"
msgstr "Stein"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a piece of the stone|{count} pieces of the stone}"
msgstr "{count|en bit av steinen|{count} biter av steinen}"

#. the thing '{count|a piece of the stone|{count} pieces of the stone}' for {thing@acc} in the
#. translations: the accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty
#. if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a piece of the stone|{count} pieces of the stone}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Runestones were raised for loved ones, and painted in bright colours."
msgstr "Runesteiner ble reist for kjære som var borte, og malt i sterke farger."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The First Snow"
msgstr "Den første snøen"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Snowflakes! Winter is near. Our store needs feed for the animals: six crates of hay and four of "
"grain. Your hold takes eight: think how to row it!"
msgstr ""
"Snøfnugg! Vinteren er nær. Lageret trenger fôr til dyrene: seks kasser høy og fire kasser korn. "
"Lasterommet {crew|ditt|ditt|deres} tar åtte: tenk ut hvordan {crew|du|du|dere} skal ro det!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hay for the sheep, the goats and Rosa. Now the grain."
msgstr "Høy til sauene, geitene og Rosa. Nå kornet."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The store is full! Let the snow come. Come in, the soup is hot."
msgstr "Lageret er fullt! La snøen komme. Kom inn, suppa er varm."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "In winter, the animals stayed in the barn for months and ate the hay of the summer."
msgstr "Om vinteren sto dyrene i fjøset i flere måneder og spiste sommerens høy."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Ice Breaks"
msgstr "Isen går"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Hear that crack? The ice breaks: spring is here again! Row out and hail two boats: ask how "
"everybody got through the winter."
msgstr ""
"Hører {crew|du|du|dere} braket? Isen går: våren er her igjen! Ro ut og hils på to båter: spør "
"hvordan alle har kommet seg gjennom vinteren."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Everybody is well! But Tova has asked for you all winter. Row to Laxön!"
msgstr "Alle har det bra! Men Tova har spurt etter {crew|deg|deg|dere} hele vinteren. Ro til Laxön!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A long winter! But the herring kept, thanks to your salt."
msgstr "En lang vinter! Men silda holdt seg, takket være saltet {crew|ditt|ditt|deres}."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"There you are! Spring is when the animals need us most. Will you be my apprentices, and learn to "
"heal?"
msgstr ""
"Der er {crew|du|du|dere}! Om våren trenger dyrene oss mest. Vil {crew|du|du|dere} bli "
"{crew|lærlingen|lærlingen|lærlingene} mine og lære å helbrede?"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "When the ice broke in spring, the boats came out, and with them the news."
msgstr "Når isen gikk om våren, kom båtene ut, og med dem nyhetene."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Coughing Horse"
msgstr "Hesten som hoster"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Your first case as healers: Ragnfrid's old horse Bror coughs. Take him this syrup of thyme and "
"honey, then come back to me after a night, to hear how he is."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Ditt|Ditt|Deres} første oppdrag som helbreder{crew|||e}: den gamle hesten til Ragnfrid, "
"Bror, hoster. Ta med denne sirupen av timian og honning til ham, og kom tilbake til meg etter en "
"natt for å høre hvordan det går."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Thyme and honey? Bror loves it. He licks the spoon!"
msgstr "Timian og honning? Det elsker Bror. Han slikker skjeen!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "He slept the whole night and coughs no more. Tell Tova: her apprentices are good!"
msgstr ""
"Han sov hele natta og hoster ikke mer. Si til Tova: {crew|lærlingen|lærlingen|lærlingene} hennes "
"er flink{crew|||e}!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Well done! You listened, you waited, you looked. That is healing."
msgstr ""
"Godt gjort! {crew|Du|Du|Dere} lyttet, {crew|du|du|dere} ventet, {crew|du|du|dere} så etter. Det er"
" helbreding."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Syrup"
msgstr "Sirup"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "the syrup"
